WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
1: Family, Identity, and History.

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.040
Welcome to Year 7 English at Ehel Academy!

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.700
This is Unit 1: Family, Identity, and History.

4
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:19.920
In this unit, you will explore some of the most important
questions a person can ask: Where do I come from?

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.880
Who are the people in my family?

6
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.840
What stories have been passed down through the generations?

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.120
You will read about families, learn
how to describe your own background,

8
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.960
and discover how people across East Africa
and the wider world have moved, settled,

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.120
and built new lives over the centuries.

10
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.740
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:49.300
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand a passage about family history and migration,

12
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.560
and discuss its ideas in english.

13
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:57.680
you will also use the past simple tense correctly
to describe completed actions and events.

14
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.160
you will also distinguish between the
past simple and the present perfect tense.

15
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.780
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:15.860
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: belligerent,
malevolence, vindictive, infuriate, animosity, narcissistic.

17
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.200
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.170
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:32.600
The reading sequence includes Family, Identity, and
History: source text 1 and Family, Identity, and History:

20
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.570
source text 2.

21
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.080
Read actively.

22
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.260
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

23
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.220
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

24
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:49.700
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

25
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:57.920
What it means and why it matters The past simple tense
is used to talk about actions or events that happened and

26
00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.040
finished in the past.

27
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.880
It is the most important tense for telling stories,
describing experiences, and talking about history.

28
00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.380
When we say "I played football yesterday" or "She went
to the market last week," we are using the past simple.

29
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:18.150
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

30
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.160
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

31
00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:28.800
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

32
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.560
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

33
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.160
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

34
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.840
You are ready to begin.

35
00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:43.860
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

36
00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.680
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

37
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
